PATCH 576: the INT-8 handler's byte rotate and chain carry, and the sound resource's relocation
callback (bdcc's CS, the c06d thunk, SOUNDDVR 01fd).

board:0026 / board:0017.  Found while giving the port the original's time base (the PIT/VGA clock in the
shim, board:0026), which made two dormant defects visible:

  30f8/31c3  `rcl BYTE PTR [0x44b],1` after `call 31c3` rotates 31c3's return carry -- the wrap of the
         BIOS-chain accumulator `add [0x18be],ax` at its tail -- into the flag byte whose bit 1 selects
         the chain to the saved INT 8 ([0x432]) and whose bit 0 skips the EOI.  Ghidra widened it to a
         WORD rotate with a constant 0 carry: the low byte of [0x44c] -- the retrace period 2fd3 had
         just measured -- lost a bit per interrupt (0x427f -> 0x42fe -> 0x42fc -> ..), and the BIOS
         tick was never chained.  Byte rotate, CF threaded through g_fist_cf (31c3's `test [0x6b] ;
         jne` early return leaves CF = 0).

  bdcc   `mov [0x9f22],cs` -- the sound descriptor's relocation callback is 0xc06d:CS.  The decompile
         stored CS = 0x1000; the oracle stores 1119:c06d (scratch/oracle/player.ram.bin, DGROUP:0x9f1c
         = cc 59 a0 03 6d c0 19 11), and with DGROUP 0x2d19 <-> 0x1c00 the oracle's 0x1119 is the
         port's segment 0 -- bdcc runs under the 0x0000 cluster.  1000:c06d is DGROUP:0x6d.
  c06d   the thunk itself was never emitted: `call cs:[bx+0xc073] ; retf`, table {c084 (kind 0: the
         block moved), c0b0 (2: [0x53c] unlock), c0b6 (4: be67), c083 x5}.  c084 = `push ax ; push dx ;
         lcall [0x538]` (SOUNDDVR 0245: lock) `; pop ; pop ; clc ; lcall [0x518]` (SOUNDDVR 01fd) `;
         jb c096` (report through [0x5c] if a song is loaded).  Ghidra dropped AX/DX and the CF.
  01fd   (fist_snd.c) SOUNDDVR "the block at AX is now at DX": es = cs:[0x831] (the driver's data
         page); es:[6] (the song segment) and es:[0] (the queued one-shot) are re-homed when they equal
         AX, CF = 0; if neither matches and either is nonzero, `int 5 ; stc`.  Ghidra read es:[6] as
         DGROUP:6 and es:[0] as host address 0.

  Effect: the menu music's block is compacted at boot (patch 575's faithful fade-buffer allocations
  move it from 0x4c61 to 0x4c31); without the callback the driver kept playing from 0x4c61 -- the
  MAINMENU.MS3 melody matched the oracle for 130 notes and then decoded garbage, and the voice chain
  read from the stale paragraphs cycled (the 0c39 hang).  With it: 239/239 notes, no hang.

